    narrative: "Maru Bihag has the tone material of Bihag but reverses its balance: tivra Ma dominates, and shuddha Ma survives only in the single phrase Sa Ma Ga, so that the raag reads as a confluence of the Kalyan and Bihag angas. Ga and Ni are pivotal, Re is articulated in descent as a meend from Sa, and Pa is sustained. The typical Bihag phrase Pa Ma(t) Ga Ma Ga is not allowed. The Raga Guide credits the sarangi player Abban Khan of Saharanpur with fixing its present form and Alladiya Khan and the Kirana gharana with popularising it; Parrikar calls it Alladiya Khan's creation outright. The name is a misnomer, since it has no relation to Maru or Marwa. It is one of the most performed night raags of the modern concert stage."
