    narrative: "Shyam Kalyan is an early-evening raag of the Kalyan thaat that carries the Kamod signature Ga Ma Pa Ga Ma Re Sa in its descent. Dha is omitted in ascent, both Madhyams are used, and Ga appears in ascent only as a grace: the rise is Re Ma(t) Pa Ni Sa', never Ga Ma Pa Ni Sa'. Pa is the vadi and Re takes the descending rest. Its nearest neighbour is Shuddha Sarang, from which it is separated by the treatment of Dha and Ga, and Parrikar reads it as a chalan-bheda within the Kalyan framework. Jitendra Abhisheki, Bade Ghulam Ali Khan and Nikhil Banerjee are among its recorded exponents."
