    narrative: "Durga is a pentatonic night raag of remarkable purity, omitting Ga and Ni entirely. This unusual choice of swaras gives Durga a wide-spaced, austere beauty — the intervals between notes are larger than most raags, and the music moves in expansive steps. The vadi Ma and samvadi Sa anchor the raag, and the Ma–Pa–Dha–Ma–Re movement gives it its devotional, Goddess-invoking quality (its name directly references Durga, the divine feminine). Performed at night, Durga carries a calm, powerful serenity — not soft but still, like a deep body of water."
