    narrative: "Pahadi is a folk raag of mountain freshness and open skies, using five core swaras in a way that evokes the north Indian hills and their musical traditions. Its rules are relatively relaxed by classical standards — other swaras may appear in ornamentation — and this flexibility gives Pahadi a free, improvisatory character that sets it apart from more rigidly defined raags. The raag's pentatonic simplicity belies its emotional range: it can be playful, wistful, or deeply lyrical depending on the performer, and it has been extraordinarily influential in Hindi film music."
