    narrative: "Mand is a folk raag from Rajasthan, sung at weddings, births and festivals such as Gangaur, and popular in light-classical settings. Its base is the Bilawal scale with all seven swaras shuddha, rendered in heavily ornamented vakra movements; some performers add mishra touches of komal Ga, komal Dha or tivra Ma, but these are colouring, not structure. It sounds natural and simple and is deceptively hard to sing well. Its character is festive and earthy, rooted in songs about love and separation in the desert landscape."
