    sources: [{"tag":"RG","url":"https://archive.org/details/ragaguideasurveyof74hindustaniragassvarnalataraoetalled.joepbar"},{"tag":"T","url":"https://tanarang.com/raag-vibhas/"}],
    narrative: "Vibhas, also spelled Bibhas, is a stark dawn raag of the Bhairav thaat using five swaras: Sa, komal Re, Ga, Pa and komal Dha, with Ga weak and Ma and Ni omitted. The absence of Ma and Ni removes much of the usual melodic texture, leaving a spare, direct emotional impact; komal Dha is the vadi and komal Re the samvadi, and the phrase Pa Dha(k) Pa with andolan on Dha is its signature. Two other raags share the name: a Marwa-thaat Bibhas with shuddha Dha, and a Purvi-thaat form, both rarer. Vibhas is heard mainly in dhrupad and in the morning repertoire of the older gharanas, and is more a meditative form than a performative one."
