    narrative: "Jogiya is a dawn raag of ascetic wandering, evoking the jogi (yogi) who roams at the boundary of night and day. Its pentatonic scale with komal Re and komal Dha creates an eerie, untethered quality — appropriate for a raag about spiritual homelessness and the search that has no earthly destination. Omitting Ga and Ni in ascent removes two of the most emotionally expressive swaras, leaving a spare, almost naked sound; Ga and Ni may be touched in descent. Jogiya is closely associated with the songs of wandering ascetics and with the last, coldest hour before sunrise."
