    narrative: "Basant Mukhari pairs the poorvang of Bhairav (komal Re, shuddha Ga and Ma) with the uttarang of Bhairavi (komal Dha and Ni), a scale equivalent to the 14th Carnatic melakarta Vakulabharanam. Despite its name it has nothing to do with Basant. Parrikar notes that no universally accepted Hindustani precepts exist for it and associates its modern form with S. N. Ratanjankar; tanarang calls it a sweet, soothing morning raag that is nevertheless difficult to render smoothly. Mathur and colleagues (2015) used it as one of their twelve test raags, where listeners rated it sad in alaap and tense in gat, the same profile as Marwa and Lalit."
