    narrative: "Sindhu Bhairavi is a lighter, more romantic shade of Bhairavi, with the same scale but a phrase vocabulary that tends toward tender sweetness rather than deep pathos. Where Bhairavi is about farewell and the weight of ending, Sindhu Bhairavi is more about the gentle sadness of longing — its mood is that of a love song rather than a funeral hymn. It is widely performed in semi-classical and thumri formats and has been the basis for many well-known film songs."
