    narrative: "Bhupali Todi, or Bhupal Todi, is the pentatonic carrier of the Todi raganga: the five swaras of Bhoop — Sa Re Ga Pa Dha — with Re, Ga and Dha all komal, and no Ma or Ni at all. It is therefore placed in the Bhairavi thaat by scale, though it is sung with Todi's low komal Ga and Todi's gravity, and many texts group it with Todi for that reason. The scale is symmetrical around Pa, and the movement Ga(k)–Pa–Dha(k) with andolan on the komal notes is its heart. It is a morning raag of spiritual purity, often used for devotional compositions, and should not be confused with Bhoopali of the Kalyan thaat."
