    narrative: "Zila Kafi is a folk-festive raag closely related to Kafi but with a lighter, more celebratory character. It is particularly associated with the Holi festival and the spring season, and its folk origins give it a flexibility and informality unusual in classical contexts. The raag is performed in thumri and dadra styles and is rarely subjected to extended alap treatment, functioning instead as a vehicle for lively, rhythmically driven compositions."
