    narrative: "Dhani is a pentatonic night raag of gentle intimacy, omitting Re and Dha and using komal Ga and komal Ni. The absence of Re removes the second degree — a swara that often provides opening and direction — creating a raag that circles inward rather than reaching outward. The characteristic Pa–Ni–Sa movement is warm and direct, and the overall character is one of quiet, personal expressiveness. Dhani is closely related to Charukeshi in some respects but has its own phrase vocabulary and a distinctly more intimate, less formally structured character."
