    narrative: "Patdeep is an afternoon raag of quiet contemplation formed by taking Bhimpalasi and replacing its komal Ni with shuddha Ni; that one substitution is the whole difference between the two. The shuddha Ni is prominent in ascent — Ni Sa Ga(k) Ma Pa Ni Sa, with Re and Dha omitted — and Pa is the vadi with Sa as samvadi. Its character is more understated than Bhimpalasi, less urgently longing and more calmly reflective, and the raised Ni gives it a lift toward Sa that Bhimpalasi's flattened Ni withholds. It embodies afternoon stillness — the inward turn of a mind at rest — and is associated with slow, meditative khayal compositions."
