    narrative: "Madhyamad Sarang is Vrindavani Sarang with a single change: it uses komal Ni only, in both ascent and descent, where Vrindavani takes shuddha Ni on the way up. Everything else — the pentatonic Sa Re Ma Pa Ni scale, the vadi Re, the summer-afternoon time — is shared, and some texts treat the two as one raag. The consistently flattened Ni gives Madhyamad Sarang a slightly more grounded, meditative quality, and its compositions lean toward the stillness of midday heat rather than the playfulness of Vrindavani."
