    narrative: "Bahar is the quintessential spring raag, associated with the season of flowering and renewal. Its komal Ga places it in the Kafi thaat, but it uses both Nishads — shuddha Ni in the ascending phrase Dha Ni Sa and komal Ni in descent — and its arohana leaps rather than climbs: Sa Ma, Pa Ga(k) Ma, Dha Ni Sa, with Re omitted in ascent. Ma is the vadi and Sa the samvadi. Bahar is most at home in festive compositions celebrating spring, Holi, and the return of warmth, and its joyful, folk-tinged character has made it one of the most beloved seasonal raags. It is often paired with Basant, the other great spring raag, and the two are combined in the jod raag Basant Bahar."
