    narrative: "Pilu is a gentle, folksy raag that defies strict classification — it is one of the most 'mishra' (mixed) raags in the tradition, where the rules are relaxed and swaras from neighboring raags appear freely in service of emotional expression. It is above all a thumri raag, and in the hands of great thumri singers it becomes a fluid, intimate vehicle for the direct expression of longing and love. Pilu is performed at any time and in any season, which itself reflects its fluid, unclassifiable nature. Its character is warm, direct, and deeply human."
