    narrative: "Nayaki Kanada is a late-night raag of the Kanada family said to have been composed by Gopal Nayak, court musician of Devagiri. Dha is omitted, which sets it apart from Darbari and most other Kanadas, and the raag lives in the upper half of the octave — it is an uttarang-pradhan raag whose phrases Ma Pa Ni(k) Pa and Ni(k) Pa Sa give it a dynamic, scintillating quality that impresses the listener immediately. The komal Ga is approached from Ma in the Kanada manner, and Pa is the vadi. Its name refers to the nayak rather than the nayika, and its character is one of enthusiasm and vitality rather than the inward softness its name is sometimes taken to suggest."
