    narrative: "Sindhura, or Saindhavi, is an old desi raag already named in the Sangita Ratnakara and, like Kafi, originating in Sind. It shares Kafi's material but omits Ga in ascent, prolongs Ga in descent, and has two routes to the upper Sa: one without Ni (Ma Pa Dha Sa') and one with a doubled shuddha Ni (Ma Pa Ni Ni Sa'). An elongated Dha and the phrase Ma Pa, Ma Ga(k) Re are what separate it from Kafi. It is an upper-register raag and a light one, at home in thumri, tappa and hori rather than khayal; Kumar Gandharva, D. V. Paluskar and Nikhil Banerjee recorded it."
