    narrative: "Abhogi is a relatively recent borrowing from Carnatic music that omits Pa and Ni. In the North it is usually rendered with Kanada movements, hence the name Abhogi Kanada: the komal Ga is approached from Ma and given a light oscillation, and the Kanada phrase Ga(k) Ma Re Sa is the usual way home to the tonic. Sa and Ma are the important notes, with Dha and Re frequently sustained, and some musicians drop Re in ascent. It resembles Bageshri, which however includes komal Ni and a limited Pa. tanarang describes a deep atmosphere that can be expanded across all three octaves; Ali Akbar Khan and Kishori Amonkar have well-known recordings."
