    narrative: "Shivranjani is a pentatonic night raag that takes the five notes of Bhoopali and flattens the Ga. That single change turns Bhoopali's warmth into something plaintive, and the raag has become the standard vehicle for pathos in Hindi film music, from 'Jaane kahan gaye woh din' onward. In classical practice it is a light, straightforward raag that can be expanded freely across the octaves; tanarang notes that it must be kept clear of Bhoopali by the treatment of Ga. Pa is the vadi and Sa the samvadi. It is conventionally filed under Kafi because of the komal Ga, though its structure has nothing of Kafi's grammar."
