    narrative: "Asavari is a morning raag of austere, detached gravity, the parent thaat raag for its family. Its characteristic vakra arohana — skipping Ga and Ni in ascent — gives it a sparse, direct quality, and the three komal swaras (Ga, Dha, Ni) in descent create a deeply melancholic, introspective sound. The vadi komal Dhaivata sits in the upper register and is the point of greatest expressiveness. Asavari is an ancient raag with roots stretching back to early Sanskrit musical treatises, and its restrained, dignified sorrow is considered one of the purest expressions of Karuna ras."
