    narrative: "Shuddha Todi is the strict, orthodox form of Todi using all the canonical alterations without any vakra movements or borrowed swaras. It is considered the purest expression of the Todi emotional world — concentrated, intense pathos without any of the ornamental complexity that characterizes Miyan ki Todi's characteristic meends and gamaks. In practice, the term often refers to the same raag as Miyan ki Todi but emphasizes a more direct, unornamented approach to the scale."
