    narrative: "Lalita Gauri is a jod raag — a double-stranded raag — that weaves the Lalit phrase using both Madhyams into the frame of Gauri, a Purvi-ang sunset raag with komal Re and komal Dha and shuddha Ma. Gauri supplies the basic theme and the twilight gravity; Lalit's Ma(t) Ma Ga is inserted at junctures to unsettle it. Some renditions take shuddha Dha, which tilts the raag toward Marwa. It was created by Kesarbai Kerkar of the Jaipur-Atrauli gharana, who made it a concert centrepiece, and differing forms survive in other khayal gharanas. It is performed at sunset, not at dawn."
