    narrative: "Puriya Dhanashri is a richly complex sunset raag of the Purvi thaat, blending the ang of Puriya with that of Dhanashri to create one of the most emotionally layered raags in the tradition. Its combination of komal Re, shuddha Ga, tivra Ma, and komal Dha creates a scale of beautiful tension. Pancham is the vadi and the centre around which the raag expands — it is weak in ascent, where the rise is Ni Re(k) Ga Ma(t) Dha(k) Ni Sa, and prominent in descent — and komal Re is the samvadi. The characteristic phrases Ma(t) Ga Ma(t) Re(k) Ga Re(k) Sa and Ni Dha(k) Pa give the raag its depth and shadow beneath its romantic character. It is considered one of the great sunset raags."
