    narrative: "Paraj is a rare raag of the last quarter of the night, sung in the hours before dawn, from the Purvi thaat. Its scale is nearly identical to Purvi and Basant but its vadi, samvadi, and phrase vocabulary create an entirely different emotional world — quieter, more personal, more introspective. The raag is considered one of the most difficult to perform convincingly precisely because its character is so understated; without careful attention to the specific phrase shapes, it collapses into Basant or Puriya Dhanashri. Paraj is a raag for the deeply initiated."
