    narrative: "Marwa is one of the most psychologically unsettling raags in the Hindustani tradition — deliberately so. The complete absence of Pa, the most grounding and stabilizing of all swaras, creates a raag without any tonal anchor. Combined with komal Re and tivra Ma, the scale contains extreme tensions that never resolve: the music reaches upward without ever finding a stable resting point. Performed at sunset, Marwa captures the restlessness and incompleteness of twilight — neither day nor night, neither resolution nor release. The vadi komal Re, sitting at the very foundation of the scale, is the primary source of the raag's distinctive tension."
