    narrative: "Puriya is a mysterious, deeply yearning sunset raag closely related to Marwa (both omit Pa and use komal Re and tivra Ma) but with its own distinctive phrase vocabulary and emotional character. Where Marwa is restless and unresolved, Puriya is more melancholic and searching — a raag of profound longing rather than existential restlessness. Its characteristic arohana begins from the lower Ni, creating a phrase that seems to emerge from depth and reach upward, and the vadi Gandhar is the site of its greatest emotional intensity."
