    narrative: "Sohini is a raag of the last quarter of the night, sung in the hours before sunrise, and it belongs to the Marwa thaat: komal Re, tivra Ma, shuddha Dha and Ni, and no Pa at all. It is an upper-octave raag — Re is omitted in ascent and the phrases gather around Dha, the vadi, and the upper Sa, with Ga as samvadi. The characteristic descent Ga Ma(t) Dha Ga Ma(t) Ga Re(k) Sa is its signature. Where Marwa and Puriya sink toward the lower Ni and komal Re, Sohini reaches upward, and its longing is bright and urgent rather than heavy. The raag is associated with the Punjabi folk tale of Sohni, who swam the Chenab each night to meet her beloved Mahiwal."
