    narrative: "Bhatiyar is a dawn raag of profound gravity, performed in the hours before sunrise. It is placed in the Marwa thaat — komal Re, shuddha Dha and Ni — but it retains Pa and uses both Madhyams, with shuddha Ma as the vadi and tivra Ma appearing in the ascending phrase Ma(t) Dha Sa. The raag is thoroughly vakra: Sa Ma, Pa Ga, Ma(t) Dha Sa in the rise, and Ni Dha Pa Ma, Pa Ga Re(k) Sa in the fall, and it is said to be learnable only from a guru. Its character is one of ancient, weighty contemplation — the darkness before dawn when the world is at its most still — and its rarity in performance has given it an almost legendary quality among connoisseurs."
