    narrative: "Saraswati is a sweet night raag imported from Carnatic music, where it is a janya of Vachaspati. Its scale omits Ga and combines tivra Ma with komal Ni — a pairing rare in Hindustani music and one that fits none of the ten thaats. Tivra Ma is the vital note, and the Pancham–Rishabh sangati is raag-vachak: Re Ma(t) Pa Dha, Sa Ni(k) Dha, Pa Ma(t) Re. Ni is usually omitted in ascent, though some musicians admit it. The character is luminous and gently devotional rather than turbulent, and the raag is performed in the night up to midnight."
