    narrative: "Charukeshi is a Carnatic raag that has found a firm foothold in Hindustani music. Its scale pairs an all-shuddha poorvang (Sa Re Ga Ma) with an all-komal uttarang (Pa Dha(k) Ni(k)), which places it outside all ten of Bhatkhande's thaats. The combination creates a raag that feels simultaneously open and shadowed, joyful and touched with pathos: komal Dha adds a tension that is quickly resolved toward Ma or Sa, and komal Ni decorates the notes around it. Its vadi Pancham anchors the music in the middle register. Charukeshi is beloved for its distinctive sound and its relative independence from strict performance-time conventions."
