    narrative: "Kirwani is a hauntingly beautiful night raag of Carnatic origin (Keeravani) that has been fully absorbed into Hindustani practice. Its scale — shuddha Re, komal Ga, shuddha Ma and Pa, komal Dha, and a shuddha Ni leading up to Sa — is identical to the Western harmonic minor, which gives it an immediately striking quality to ears trained in either tradition. The pairing of komal Ga with shuddha Ni fits none of Bhatkhande's ten thaats, and Bhatkhande did not list it. The tension between the shadowed komal Dha and the bright leading Ni creates a raag of beautiful ambiguity — romantic and slightly melancholic at once. Kirwani is relatively modern in the Hindustani repertoire but has become extremely popular, particularly among instrumentalists."
